{"id": "46ca00f4-f298-44ee-933f-e22271dd4b4e", "title": "Safety Stock Optimization for CPG", "text": "Safety stock for CPG products must account for demand variability (CV), supplier lead time variability, and target service level. Formula: SS = Z \u00d7 \u03c3_LT \u00d7 D\u0304 where Z=1.65 for 95% service level, \u03c3_LT is std dev of lead time demand, D\u0304 is average daily demand. For fast-moving items like Shampoo Pro and Detergent Powder, safety stock of 15-20 days is recommended under normal conditions, increasing to 30-45 days during identified supply risk events. Dynamic safety stock models should incorporate real-time event triggers from supply chain intelligence feeds. [Source: CPG Industry Intelligence Report Q4 2024, Confidence: 0.93]", "metadata": {"type": "intelligence_article"}}
