{"id": "1a9bf6ba-67db-48cf-a078-60a91c109f50", "title": "Event-Triggered Demand Sensing", "text": "Traditional demand forecasting (ARIMA, exponential smoothing) fails to capture exogenous supply chain shocks. Modern CPG supply chain intelligence integrates event triggers: tariff announcements cause 10-30% demand spikes as retailers pre-buy; route closures cause 5-20% demand suppression due to shelf-out; war disruptions cause 25-60% demand surges for essential categories. Event trigger taxonomy: Level-1 (monitor), Level-2 (prepare alternate source), Level-3 (activate emergency procurement), Level-4 (force majeure). ML models trained on event-demand pairs achieve 15-25% better MAPE vs baseline for disruption periods. [Source: CPG Industry Intelligence Report Q3 2024, Confidence: 0.9]", "metadata": {"type": "intelligence_article"}}
