{"id": "95390da8-7ea0-4432-9b7b-ed0b1234c9e1", "title": "Tariff Impact Assessment Framework", "text": "When tariffs are announced, CPG supply chain teams must execute: (1) SKU-level cost impact analysis within 48h \u2014 map each SKU to HS codes and calculate landed cost change. (2) Alternate sourcing feasibility \u2014 identify countries with preferential trade agreements (FTA). (3) Pre-build analysis \u2014 calculate optimal inventory build quantity: Q* = min(storage_capacity, demand_forecast \u00d7 coverage_days). (4) Price elasticity modeling \u2014 determine how much cost can be passed to consumer vs absorbed. (5) Hedge procurement for 6-12 months where shelf life permits. Affected categories in CPG: personal care (high chemical content = high tariff sensitivity), packaged foods (agricultural commodity input sensitivity). [Source: CPG Industry Intelligence Report Q3 2024, Confidence: 0.88]", "metadata": {"type": "intelligence_article"}}
